# declared skips for the riscv32 column. one entry per line:
#   <case-glob>  <layers>[:<profiles>]  <reason>
# layers is any of a, b, c, or * for all three. naming pipelines after a colon
# declares away those cells and no others. a skip counts as a skip in the matrix,
# never as a pass, and the run fails on an empty cell that has no entry here.
#
# layer c needs no entry: engines.conf declares engine none for this target, which
# the matrix reports as its own label.

* ab the riscv32 backend does not legalize 64-bit values, so no case can be built for it: a u64 move refuses with "legalize: operation wider than the target ALU is unsupported (MIR_MOV, 8 bytes wide)" and a u64 shift with "legalize: shift through an unsupported operand shape on this target (MIR_SHR_U, 8 bytes wide)". every case folds a u64 checksum, so this is the whole column. the register-pair lowering that closes it is the same work that would give this target an execution engine.
